\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{The displacement of a joint sign line}
\date{2026-11-27}

\p{In the pole expression of \ref{fdip-01C7}, equal endpoint signs give #{a-\ui\sin x}. Damping its imaginary part keeps its real part equal to #{a}. Opposite signs give #{a\cos x-\ui\sin x=a\ue^{-\ui a x}}. The equal-sign line acts without translation and the opposite-sign line translates by the power #{-a} of #{X} in the [ordered evaluation](fdip-01C3). In both cases the exponent is half the final sign minus half the initial sign, #{(b-a)/2}.}
